    "Single source of truth for legacy URL redirects, migrated 1:1 from the former vercel.json.",
    "Sources use Cloudflare _redirects syntax: `*` matches any number of segments (exposed as :splat),",
    "`:name` matches exactly one segment and never matches a trailing slash.",
    "Rules are evaluated top to bottom; the first match wins. Keep them in the order vercel.json",
    "used so the legacy-redirects Worker reproduces the old behaviour exactly.",
    "Entries without `host` apply to insbs.net and are compiled into public/_redirects by",
    "scripts/generate-cloudflare-redirects.ts, which moves exact-path rules ahead of pattern rules to",
    "fit Cloudflare's 100-pattern-rule budget and fails if that reordering would change any answer.",
    "Entries with `host` are evaluated by the legacy-redirects Worker in workers/legacy-redirects and",
    "always resolve against https://insbs.net."
